  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ExtraCECI: A cluster randomised controlled trial of community-based person-centred enhanced care for people with HIV/AIDS in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. To establish a patient and public involvement (PPI) person-centred network of People Living With HIV/AIDS (PLWHA) support groups and stakeholders to inform research procedures and dissemination throughout the project implementation

2. To refine the community-based enhanced care intervention (adding an extra component to become &apos;ExtraCECI&apos;) with related training materials and assessment tools prior to effectiveness evaluation

3. To evaluate the effectiveness of ExtraCECI to improve quality of life and person-centred outcomes for PLWHA compared to standard HIV care

4. To assess the cost-effectiveness of ExtraCECI compared to standard HIV care and describe the implications for Ghana Health Services&apos; resource management

5. To conduct a process evaluation using all data sources to identify what worked, for whom, why, and in what circumstances</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MRC AGHRB award to conduct a cluster randomised controlled trial to evaluate the effectiveness of a community based enhanced care intervention (CECI) to improve quality of life and person-centred outcomes for people living with HIV/AIDS in Ghana.</narrative>
  </description>
